		{"id":"c100c33caf600efb","type":"text","text":"- Observation on the texture and surface area of the soil. Clay particles hold the most nutrients then silt then sand. biochar, perlite, vermiculite, gravel, and rocks are other presences which can effect nutrient retention and leaching. Roots of course increase nutrient capacity. \n- Cation exchange capacity testing","x":1640,"y":291,"width":420,"height":249},
